maluos-gateway (0.6.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 3, shared inference across the estate
    (docs/phase13-slice3-inference.md): the `estate` backend kind, a rung
    per backend the directory publishes to this host (the cache the
    enrolment side keeps under /run/maluos/estate or /run/maluos/office),
    dialled over the overlay with this host's own inference key; the estate
    rungs join the tiers that name their models and rank by the kernel's
    priority then the serving host's expected wait; X-MaluOS-Prefer: estate.
    The serving side accepts an estate member's inference key against the
    peers the kernel published (the principal node:<ref>), applies its class
    and classification ceilings, never spends its cloud credit for it, and
    refuses not_shared with a retry_after while the idle rule holds the
    switch off. With the scheduler entitlement the gateway asks the kernel
    to place a call first (300 ms) and falls back to its own ranking; the
    route says placed or ranked. The envelope travels on forwarded calls;
    GET /v1/maluos/inference answers this host's facts for its heartbeat;
    maluctl gateway estate [refresh]; chat --prefer --sensitivity --envelope.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0000

